---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { getDeal } from "../data/products";
import { formatPrice, formatPercentage } from "../lib/format";
import { relativeHref, ROUTES } from "../lib/site";

const pretzel = getDeal("43666515");
const airFryer = getDeal("43624515");
const path = Astro.url.pathname;

const currentSort = ["Price: Low to high", "Price: High to low", "New", "Relevance"];
const redesignSort = ["Biggest discount", "Biggest saving"];
---

<Layout
  title="Why this redesign"
  description="The grounded evidence behind MARKDOWN: what Kmart's own Clearance sort menu offers today, and why percentage discount and dollar saving need separate sort modes."
>
  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">The reasoning, grounded</p>
      <h1>Why this redesign</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Everything below is drawn from a direct browser screenshot of Kmart's own live Clearance
        range, plus the 11 grounded product pages used in the <a
          href={relativeHref(path, ROUTES.dealExplorer)}>Deal Explorer</a
        >. Nothing here is invented.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Current sorting vs. redesign sorting</h2>
      <div class="compare-grid">
        <div class="compare-col compare-current">
          <p class="compare-label">Kmart Clearance today</p>
          <ul>
            {currentSort.map((option) => <li>{option}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <p class="compare-note">Confirmed by screenshot — no other sort option is offered.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-col compare-redesign">
          <p class="compare-label">MARKDOWN adds</p>
          <ul>
            {redesignSort.map((option) => <li>{option}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <p class="compare-note">
            Computed from each product's own <code>originalPrice</code> and
            <code>clearancePrice</code>, never hand-entered.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight scale-section">
    <div class="container scale-grid">
      <div class="scale-number" aria-hidden="true">10,000</div>
      <div>
        <h2>10,000 products, one sort axis</h2>
        <blockquote>“1–60 of 10000 Products”</blockquote>
        <p>
          That count is Kmart's own, read directly off the live Clearance listing. With a
          catalogue that size and only <em>price</em>, <em>recency</em>, or <em>relevance</em> to
          sort by, a genuinely deep markdown has no way to surface itself — it's easy for it to
          sit on page 40, buried among items that were already inexpensive. Sorting by markdown
          strength instead turns that same catalogue into something worth skimming.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Percentage discount and dollar saving are different questions</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Ranking the same 11 grounded products by percentage off, versus by dollars off, puts
        different items first — using their real, screenshot-confirmed prices:
      </p>

      <div class="example-grid">
        <article class="example-card">
          <p class="compare-label">Sorted by biggest discount</p>
          <h3>{pretzel.name}</h3>
          <p class="example-stat">{formatPercentage(pretzel.discountPercentage)} off</p>
          <p class="example-sub">
            {formatPrice(pretzel.originalPrice)} → {formatPrice(pretzel.clearancePrice)}, saving only
            {formatPrice(pretzel.savingAmount)}
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="example-card">
          <p class="compare-label">Sorted by biggest saving</p>
          <h3>{airFryer.name}</h3>
          <p class="example-stat">{formatPrice(airFryer.savingAmount)} saved</p>
          <p class="example-sub">
            {formatPrice(airFryer.originalPrice)} → {formatPrice(airFryer.clearancePrice)}, only about
            {formatPercentage(airFryer.discountPercentage)} off
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p>
        Neither ordering is wrong — a deep percentage cut and a large dollar saving are both
        genuine markdown strength, just answering different questions. Kmart's current sort menu
        can express neither.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .compare-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (width >= 700px) {
    .compare-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .compare-col {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--paper-raised);
  }

  .compare-redesign {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }

  .compare-label {
    font-weight: 800;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .compare-col ul {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }

  .compare-col li {
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .compare-note {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .scale-section {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .scale-section h2 {
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .scale-section blockquote {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .scale-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (width >= 800px) {
    .scale-grid {
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    }
  }

  .scale-number {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 10vw, 6rem);
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .example-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  @media (width >= 700px) {
    .example-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .example-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }

  .example-card h3 {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .example-stat {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
  }

  .example-sub {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
